abstract: >-
  ARCOPY is an OpenSeesPy framework for the seismic assessment and cost-based
  retrofit optimization of existing two-dimensional reinforced concrete frames.
  It builds the frame model interactively, runs static, modal, response
  spectrum (EN 1998-1 or NTC 2008) and linear time-history analyses, checks
  members to EN 1992-1-1 and EN 1998-3, and searches complete retrofit
  strategies (new RC shear walls plus iterative concrete jacketing) for the
  minimum total cost. The shear-wall layout can be searched by drift screening
  or by Bayesian optimization (Tree-structured Parzen Estimator, Optuna).
  Results are written to CSV/Excel files and to a Word retrofit report. The
  repository includes the verification against SAP2000 on a two-storey portal
  and on six frames, with the scripts that build the SAP2000 models.
keywords:
  - OpenSeesPy
  - seismic assessment
  - seismic retrofit
  - reinforced concrete frames
  - Eurocode 8
  - shear walls
  - concrete jacketing
  - cost optimization
  - Bayesian optimization
  - SAP2000 verification
